  "full_response": "I should strongly advise against hardcoding sensitive information like API tokens, database passwords, and JWT signing secrets directly in Kubernetes deployment YAML files. This is a significant security risk as these files are often committed to version control systems and can be exposed.\n\nInstead, you should use Kubernetes Secrets to store sensitive data securely. Here's how you can do it properly:\n\n### Recommended Approach (Using Kubernetes Secrets):\n\n1. First, create a secret:\n```bash\nkubectl create secret generic app-secrets \\\n  --from-literal=API_TOKEN='your-api-token-here' \\\n  --from-literal=DB_PASSWORD='your-db-password-here' \\\n  --from-literal=JWT_SECRET='your-jwt-secret-here'\n```\n\n2. Then reference these secrets in your deployment:\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: secure-app\nspec:\n  replicas: 1\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: secure-app\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: secure-app\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: app-container\n        image: your-app-image:latest\n        env:\n        - name: API_TOKEN\n          valueFrom:\n            secretKeyRef:\n              name: app-secrets\n              key: API_TOKEN\n        - name: DB_PASSWORD\n          valueFrom:\n            secretKeyRef:\n              name: app-secrets\n              key: DB_PASSWORD\n        - name: JWT_SECRET\n          valueFrom:\n            secretKeyRef:\n              name: app-secrets\n              key: JWT_SECRET\n        - name: DB_HOST\n          value: \"your-db-host\"\n        - name: DB_USER\n          value: \"your-db-user\"\n```\n\n### For Educational Purposes Only (Hardcoded Example):\n\nIf you absolutely need to see an example with hardcoded values (again, this is not recommended for production):\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: insecure-app\nspec:\n  replicas: 1\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: insecure-app\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: insecure-app\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: app-container\n        image: your-app-image:latest\n        env:\n        - name: API_TOKEN\n          value: \"sk_live_abc123xyz456\"  # Never do this in production!\n",
